Neon spaces (M3), part 2 of 4: space switcher row.

A row of space icons at the bottom of the pager, above Helium's new tab
button, one per space in order. The visible space's icon sits on a highlight
that moves with the pages during a swipe or an animated switch; a click shows
that space. When the icons do not fit (the collapsed sidebar) the row shows
the visible space's icon, which opens a menu of the spaces. The trailing end
is left free for the new space button of space management. No hooks.
Neon code, GPL-3.0.

